  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Red Rock** (1 review): Reviewer lists this song as Red Rocking Chair [3]\n- **Fox** (1 review): Reviewer gives the full title as Home of the Red Fox, played into Georgia Mail [3]\n- **Muddy Waters Take My Pain Away** (1 review): Reviewer says the closing song is really titled Meet Me at the Creek, not the listed title [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Introduction By Ryan Beach**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **PYR**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Mystery Train**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **Taken That Slow Train**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Red Rock**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Fox**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **These Ol' Blues**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- **Seymour**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2017-05-13.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 16 songs; 92 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Lindsay Lou joined Billy on Midnight on the Stormy Deep, which falls between Georgia Mail and Freeborn Man [3]\n- Billy and Lindsay Lou sing a vocal duet during the set [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2017-05-13.flac16**: taped by Z-Man; source: Schoeps CCM4V's>Lunatec V2>Benchmark AD2K> Sound Devices 722 [1]. Also: Recorded with FOB/DFC/KFC/ZFC/AARP microphone setup, 45 feet from the stage and 6.5 feet high; Chain: Sound Devices 722 to Sound Forge 10.0 to CD Wave to 16-bit FLAC [1]",
